IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg4-s212-voting-proxies`
IMPORT `dg4-s216-quorum-vote`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law (8 Del. C. ch. 1), section 215: voting rights of members of nonstock corporations; quorum;
-- proxies. Layer 1, from the text alone. Quote lines are copied from de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt by script.
--
-- This module also holds the applicability rules of Subchapter VII for the kinds of corporation (stock, and the three kinds of
-- nonstock corporation of s 114(d)): s 215(a) for ss 211 to 214 and 216, and, for ss 217, 218 and 219, the part of s 114(b)(2)
-- and (c)(2) that says whether the stockholder-to-member reading of s 114(a) applies (src:200-207 of the same text file, which
-- is piece dg1's range; only those lines were read for this). Where a rule of ss 215(b) to (f) is the same rule as one of
-- ss 212 or 216 with members for stockholders, it calls that rule.

§ `s 215 Voting rights of members of nonstock corporations; quorum; proxies`

§§ `s 215(a) What applies to a nonstock corporation, and how it is read`

-- Sections 211 through 214 and 216 do not apply to nonstock corporations, except that s 211(a) and (d) and s 212(c), (d)
-- and (e) apply to them.
-- src:799 | Sections 211 through 214 and 216 of this title shall not apply to nonstock corporations, except that § 211(a) and (d) of this title and § 212(c), (d), and (e) of this title shall apply to such corporations, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(a) (src:799)
DECLARE `s 215(a) Provision of ss 211 to 214 and 216` IS ONE OF
    `section 211(a) of this title`
    `section 211(b) of this title`
    `section 211(c) of this title`
    `section 211(d) of this title`
    `section 211(e) of this title`
    `section 212(a) of this title`
    `section 212(b) of this title`
    `section 212(c) of this title`
    `section 212(d) of this title`
    `section 212(e) of this title`
    `section 213 of this title`
    `section 214 of this title`
    `section 216 of this title`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(a) (src:799)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 215(a) Provision of ss 211 to 214 and 216`
      kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215(a) the provision applies to the corporation` provision kind MEANS
    IF `the kind is a stock corporation` kind
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER provision
         WHEN `section 211(a) of this title` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `section 211(d) of this title` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `section 212(c) of this title` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `section 212(d) of this title` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `section 212(e) of this title` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE

-- When they apply, all references to stockholders are deemed to refer to members and all references to the board of directors
-- to the governing body; all references to stock, capital stock or shares are deemed to refer to memberships of a nonprofit
-- nonstock corporation and to membership interests of any other nonstock corporation.
-- src:799 | and, when so applied, all references therein to stockholders and to the board of directors shall be deemed to refer to the members and the governing body of a nonstock corporation, respectively; and all references to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof shall be deemed to refer to memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation and to membership interests of any other nonstock corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(a) (src:799)
DECLARE `s 215(a) What a reference to stock is read as` IS ONE OF
    `stock, capital stock or shares of a corporation authorized to issue capital stock`
    `memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation`
    `membership interests of a nonstock corporation that is not a nonprofit nonstock corporation`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(a) (src:799)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A `s 215(a) What a reference to stock is read as`
`s 215(a) a reference to stock, capital stock or shares is read as` kind MEANS
    IF `the kind is a stock corporation` kind
    THEN `stock, capital stock or shares of a corporation authorized to issue capital stock`
    ELSE IF `the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` kind
         THEN `memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation`
         ELSE `membership interests of a nonstock corporation that is not a nonprofit nonstock corporation`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(a) (src:799)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A `Actor`
`s 215(a) a reference to stockholders is read as` kind MEANS
    IF `the kind is a stock corporation` kind
    THEN `a stockholder`
    ELSE `a member of a nonstock corporation`

DECLARE `s 215(a) What a reference to the board of directors is read as` IS ONE OF
    `the board of directors of a corporation authorized to issue capital stock`
    `the governing body of a nonstock corporation`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(a) (src:799)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A `s 215(a) What a reference to the board of directors is read as`
`s 215(a) a reference to the board of directors is read as` kind MEANS
    IF `the kind is a stock corporation` kind
    THEN `the board of directors of a corporation authorized to issue capital stock`
    ELSE `the governing body of a nonstock corporation`

§§ `s 215(b) Votes and proxies of members`

-- Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws, and subject to subsection (f), each member is
-- entitled at every meeting of members to 1 vote on each matter submitted to a vote of members. The member may exercise the
-- voting rights in person or by proxy, but no proxy shall be voted on after 3 years from its date, unless the proxy provides
-- for a longer period.
-- src:800 | (b) Unless otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of a nonstock corporation, and subject to subsection (f) of this section, each member shall be entitled at every meeting of members to 1 vote on each matter submitted to a vote of members. A member may exercise such voting rights in person or by proxy, but no proxy shall be voted on after 3 years from its date, unless the proxy provides for a longer period.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(b) (src:800)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide for a number of votes other than 1 for the member on a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes they give the member on the matter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215(b) the number of votes the member is entitled to on each matter` `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide for a number of votes other than 1 for the member on a matter` `the number of votes they give the member on the matter` MEANS
    IF `the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws provide for a number of votes other than 1 for the member on a matter`
    THEN `the number of votes they give the member on the matter`
    ELSE 1

-- The member's proxy is under the same three-year limit as a stockholder's under s 212(b), and is called the same way.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(b) (src:800)
GIVEN `the date of the proxy` IS A DATE
      `the proxy provides for a longer period than 3 years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of that longer period, if it has one` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the proxy would be voted on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215(b) the three-year limit does not stop the member's proxy being voted on` `the date of the proxy` `the proxy provides for a longer period than 3 years` `the last day of that longer period, if it has one` `the day the proxy would be voted on` MEANS
    `s 212(b) the three-year limit does not stop the proxy being voted or acted upon` `the date of the proxy` `the proxy provides for a longer period than 3 years` `the last day of that longer period, if it has one` `the day the proxy would be voted on`

§§ `s 215(c) Quorum and vote of members`

-- Unless otherwise provided in this chapter, the certificate of incorporation or bylaws may specify the number of members having
-- voting power who shall be present or represented by proxy at a meeting to constitute a quorum, and the votes necessary for the
-- transaction of any business. In the absence of such specification, (1) one-third of the members constitute a quorum. A
-- specified quorum is a quorum as specified: unlike s 216, no floor of 1/3 is stated here.
-- src:801 | Unless otherwise provided in this chapter, the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of a nonstock corporation may specify the number of members having voting power who shall be present or represented by proxy at any meeting in order to constitute a quorum for, and the votes that shall be necessary for, the transaction of any business. In the absence of such specification in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws of a nonstock corporation:
-- src:802 | (1) One-third of the members of such corporation shall constitute a quorum at a meeting of such members;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(c) (src:801); § 215(c)(1) (src:802)
GIVEN `the number of members the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws require to be present or represented by proxy, if they specify one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the number of members entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members present in person or represented by proxy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(c)(1) a quorum of members is present` `the number of members the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws require to be present or represented by proxy, if they specify one` `the number of members entitled to vote at the meeting` `the number of members present in person or represented by proxy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number of members the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws require to be present or represented by proxy, if they specify one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        `the vote carries` (`at least` (1 DIVIDED BY 3) `of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) `the number of members present in person or represented by proxy` `the number of members entitled to vote at the meeting`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN
        IF `the number of members entitled to vote at the meeting` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN `the vote carries` (`at least` (specified DIVIDED BY `the number of members entitled to vote at the meeting`) `of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) `the number of members present in person or represented by proxy` `the number of members entitled to vote at the meeting`
        ELSE NOTHING

-- (2) In all matters other than the election of the governing body, the affirmative vote of a majority of the members present
-- in person or represented by proxy at the meeting and entitled to vote on the subject matter is the act of the members, unless
-- the vote of a greater number is required by this chapter. The certificate or bylaws may specify the votes necessary; the
-- order is the same as in s 216: what the chapter requires, then what the certificate or bylaws specify, then the default.
-- src:803 | (2) In all matters other than the election of the governing body of such corporation, the affirmative vote of a majority of such members present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting and entitled to vote on the subject matter shall be the act of the members, unless the vote of a greater number is required by this chapter;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(c)(2) (src:803)
GIVEN `the vote this chapter requires for the specified action, if it requires one` IS A MAYBE `Vote requirement` -- out of range: the section that requires it (pieces dg1 to dg11)
      `the vote the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws specify, if they specify one` IS A MAYBE `Vote requirement`
      `the number of votes in favor` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes of the members entitled to vote` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes present in person or represented by proxy and entitled to vote on the subject matter` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes cast` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(c)(2) the matter other than the election of the governing body is the act of the members` `the vote this chapter requires for the specified action, if it requires one` `the vote the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws specify, if they specify one` `the number of votes in favor` `the number of votes of the members entitled to vote` `the number of votes present in person or represented by proxy and entitled to vote on the subject matter` `the number of votes cast` MEANS
    `s 216(2) the matter is the act of the stockholders`
        (`s 216 the vote that is necessary for a matter other than the election of directors` `the vote this chapter requires for the specified action, if it requires one` `the vote the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws specify, if they specify one`)
        `the number of votes in favor`
        `the number of votes of the members entitled to vote`
        `the number of votes present in person or represented by proxy and entitled to vote on the subject matter`
        `the number of votes cast`

-- (3) Members of the governing body are elected by a plurality of the votes of the members present in person or represented by
-- proxy at the meeting and entitled to vote on the election.
-- src:804 | (3) Members of the governing body shall be elected by a plurality of the votes of the members of the corporation present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting and entitled to vote thereon; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(c)(3) (src:804)
GIVEN `the votes for the candidate` IS A NUMBER
      `the votes for each other candidate` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the number of members of the governing body to be elected` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(c)(3) the candidate is elected to the governing body by a plurality of the votes` `the votes for the candidate` `the votes for each other candidate` `the number of members of the governing body to be elected` MEANS
    `s 216(3) the candidate is elected by a plurality of the votes` `the votes for the candidate` `the votes for each other candidate` `the number of members of the governing body to be elected`

-- (4) Where a separate vote by a class or group is required, a majority of the members of the class or group, present in
-- person or represented by proxy, constitute a quorum entitled to take action on that matter; and in all matters other than the
-- election of members of the governing body, the affirmative vote of the majority of the members of the class or group present
-- is the act of the class or group.
-- src:805 | (4) Where a separate vote by a class or group or classes or groups is required, a majority of the members of such class or group or classes or groups, present in person or represented by proxy, shall constitute a quorum entitled to take action with respect to that vote on that matter and, in all matters other than the election of members of the governing body, the affirmative vote of the majority of the members of such class or group or classes or groups present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting shall be the act of such class or group or classes or groups.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(c)(4) (src:805)
GIVEN `the number of members of the class or group` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those members present in person or represented by proxy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(c)(4) the class or group has a quorum entitled to take action on the matter` `the number of members of the class or group` `the number of those members present in person or represented by proxy` MEANS
    `s 216(4) the class or series has a quorum entitled to take action on the matter` `the number of members of the class or group` `the number of those members present in person or represented by proxy`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(c)(4) (src:805)
GIVEN `the number of members of the class or group present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those members in favor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(c)(4) the matter is the act of the class or group` `the number of members of the class or group present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting` `the number of those members in favor` MEANS
    `s 216(4) the matter is the act of the class or series` `the number of members of the class or group present in person or represented by proxy at the meeting` `the number of those members in favor`

§§ `s 215(d) An election of the governing body not held on the designated day`

-- If the election of the governing body is not held on the day designated by the bylaws, the governing body shall cause it to be
-- held as soon thereafter as convenient.
-- src:806 | If the election of the governing body of any nonstock corporation shall not be held on the day designated by the bylaws, the governing body shall cause the election to be held as soon thereafter as convenient. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(d) (src:806)
GIVEN `the election was not held on the day designated by the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215(d) the governing body must cause the election to be held as soon thereafter as convenient` `the election was not held on the day designated by the bylaws` MEANS
    `the election was not held on the day designated by the bylaws`

-- The failure to hold the election at the designated time shall not work any forfeiture or dissolution of the corporation.
-- src:806 | The failure to hold such an election at the designated time shall not work any forfeiture or dissolution of the corporation, but the Court of Chancery may summarily order such an election to be held upon the application of any member of the corporation. At any election pursuant to such order the persons entitled to vote in such election who shall be present at such meeting, either in person or by proxy, shall constitute a quorum for such meeting, notwithstanding any provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of the corporation to the contrary.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(d) (src:806)
GIVEN `the election was not held at the designated time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(d) the failure to hold the election at the designated time works a forfeiture or dissolution of the corporation` `the election was not held at the designated time` MEANS
    IF `the election was not held at the designated time`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The Court of Chancery may summarily order the election to be held upon the application of any member. Unlike s 211(c), the
-- text names no waiting period.
-- src:806 | but the Court of Chancery may summarily order such an election to be held upon the application of any member of the corporation. At any election pursuant to such order the persons entitled to vote in such election who shall be present at such meeting, either in person or by proxy, shall constitute a quorum for such meeting, notwithstanding any provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of the corporation to the contrary.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(d) (src:806)
GIVEN `the election was not held on the day designated by the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person applying is a member of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215(d) the Court of Chancery may summarily order the election to be held` `the election was not held on the day designated by the bylaws` `the person applying is a member of the corporation` MEANS
        `the election was not held on the day designated by the bylaws`
    AND `the person applying is a member of the corporation`

-- At an election the Court orders, the persons entitled to vote who are present, in person or by proxy, constitute a quorum,
-- notwithstanding any provision of the certificate or bylaws to the contrary. With no one present the text names no quorum.
-- src:806 | At any election pursuant to such order the persons entitled to vote in such election who shall be present at such meeting, either in person or by proxy, shall constitute a quorum for such meeting, notwithstanding any provision of the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of the corporation to the contrary.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(d) (src:806)
GIVEN `the number of persons entitled to vote who are present at the election in person or by proxy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(d) the persons entitled to vote who are present constitute a quorum at the election the Court ordered` `the number of persons entitled to vote who are present at the election in person or by proxy` MEANS
    IF `the number of persons entitled to vote who are present at the election in person or by proxy` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 215(e) Electronic ballots`

-- src:807 | (e) If authorized by the governing body, any requirement of a written ballot shall be satisfied by a ballot submitted by electronic transmission, provided that any such electronic transmission must either set forth or be submitted with information from which it can be determined that the electronic transmission was authorized by the member or proxy holder.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(e) (src:807)
GIVEN `the governing body has authorized ballots by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electronic transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information from which it can be determined that it was authorized by the member or proxy holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215(e) a ballot submitted by electronic transmission satisfies any requirement of a written ballot` `the governing body has authorized ballots by electronic transmission` `the electronic transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information from which it can be determined that it was authorized by the member or proxy holder` MEANS
        `the governing body has authorized ballots by electronic transmission`
    AND `the electronic transmission sets forth, or is submitted with, information from which it can be determined that it was authorized by the member or proxy holder`

§§ `s 215(f) The record date`

-- Except as otherwise provided in the certificate, in the bylaws or by resolution of the governing body, the record date for any
-- meeting or corporate action is deemed to be the date of the meeting or action; but no record date may precede any action by
-- the governing body fixing the record date.
-- src:808 | (f) Except as otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation, in the bylaws, or by resolution of the governing body, the record date for any meeting or corporate action shall be deemed to be the date of such meeting or corporate action; provided, however, that no record date may precede any action by the governing body fixing such record date.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(f) (src:808)
GIVEN `the record date the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or a resolution of the governing body provides` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day of the meeting or corporate action` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 215(f) the record date for the meeting or corporate action` `the record date the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or a resolution of the governing body provides` `the day of the meeting or corporate action` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the record date the certificate of incorporation, the bylaws or a resolution of the governing body provides`
    WHEN JUST provided THEN provided
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day of the meeting or corporate action`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 215(f) (src:808)
GIVEN `the day proposed as the record date` IS A DATE
      `the day of the action of the governing body fixing the record date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215(f) the record date does not precede the action of the governing body fixing it` `the day proposed as the record date` `the day of the action of the governing body fixing the record date` MEANS
    `the day proposed as the record date` AT LEAST `the day of the action of the governing body fixing the record date`

§§ `s 114(b)(2) and (c)(2), as they bear on ss 217, 218 and 219: whether the section applies to the kind of corporation`

-- Section 114(a) reads references to stockholders as members for a nonstock corporation, except as (b) and (c) provide. (b)(2)
-- takes ss 211 to 214, 216 and 219 out of that reading; (c)(2) takes ss 217 and 218(a) and (b) out of it for a nonprofit nonstock
-- corporation. A section taken out of the reading, and not saved by its own terms (s 215(a) saves parts of ss 211, 212), has no
-- stockholders to speak of in a nonstock corporation: it does not apply. This is this piece's reading of s 114 (fork F-N); the
-- text of s 114 belongs to piece dg1.
-- src:200 | (b) Subsection (a) of this section shall not apply to:
-- src:202 | (2) Sections 102(f), 109(b) (last sentence), 151, 152, 153, 155, 156, 157(e), 158, 161, 162, 163, 164, 165, 166, 167, 168, 203, 211, 212, 213, 214, 216, 219, 222, 231, 243, 244, 251, 252, 267, 274, 275, 324, 364, 366(a), 391 and 502(a)(5) of this title; and
-- src:204 | (c) In the case of a nonprofit nonstock corporation, subsection (a) of this section shall not apply to:
-- src:206 | (2) Sections 102(b)(3), 111(a)(2) and (3), 144(a)(2), 217, 218(a) and (b), and 262 of this title; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(b)(2) (src:202); § 114(c)(2) (src:206)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 217 the section applies to the kind of corporation` kind MEANS
    NOT (`the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` kind)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(c)(2) (src:206)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 218(a) and (b) apply to the kind of corporation` kind MEANS
    NOT (`the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` kind)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(c)(2) (src:206)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 218(c) and (d) apply to the kind of corporation` kind MEANS
    TRUE

@ref 8 Del. C. § 114(b)(2) (src:202)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 219 the section applies to the kind of corporation` kind MEANS
    `the kind is a stock corporation` kind
